 "builder_notes": [
  "State = full questionText (from /questions/{id}; the list endpoint truncates at 255 chars), HTML stripped, leading 'To ask the <office>,' clause removed (fixed office list; records with an unknown leading form are skipped). 'To ask His Majesty's Government ...' (Lords) kept verbatim.",
  "Department names, minister titles and standard short names/acronyms of ALL 20 label bodies (not only the gold), and of the superseded DBT/DSIT/DCMS(217), replaced by '[DEPARTMENT]' (logged in meta.redactions), so a name never marks a non-gold option or points to a successor.",
  "Labels = answeringBodyId. Same-id renames merged under the latest name. Bodies superseded by the July 2026 machinery-of-government change (DBT 214, DSIT 216, DCMS 217; no question after 2026-07-14) dropped with their questions, because their successors (DBIST 220, DDCMS 10) are in the option set.",
  "Top 20 answering bodies by frequency in the frozen snapshot (tie-break random.Random(3)); stratified 7-8 per body, remainder by seeded order; one item per asking member per body where possible.",
  "Round-robin filter: a question is dropped if the same member tabled a near-identical question (token Jaccard >= 0.6 or same normalised text) to a different answering body, since the body cannot be told from the text.",
  "Dedupe: exact normalised text across the task; near-identical (token Jaccard >= 0.6 or containment) questions by the same member within a body.",
  "Card definitions: GOV.UK organisation page body paragraphs minus the 'is a ministerial department, supported by N agencies' boilerplate. 'Women and Equalities' uses the GOV.UK Office for Equality and Opportunity page (the office that supports the Minister for Women and Equalities)."
 ]
